{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Revise the T10 (overlay-infra) rubric to partition its scope away from the transient de-risking phase, so the durable-infrastructure and transient-experiment phases are disjoint. There is no runtime cross-criterion suppression by design, so the boundary must live in T10's own rubric text.\n\n## Work\n- Edit `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T10.md`: add this scope clause near the top: \"This overlay evaluates the DURABLE infrastructure — the IaC/config that persists. Transient, throwaway experiments used to de-risk a mechanism before committing it — their creation, isolation, and teardown — are out of scope here.\"\n- Keep the rubric independent: T10 must not name T15 or reference ownership by another overlay.\n- Add an observable regression fixture for a plan whose only infrastructure is an explicitly throwaway experiment that is created, probed, and torn down.\n- Regenerate `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` from the registry.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The T10 rubric contains the durable-infrastructure scope clause.\n- [ ] The T10 rubric does not name T15 or assign scope to another overlay.\n- [ ] A regression test proves that a plan whose only infrastructure is an explicitly throwaway experiment does not receive a T10 prevent-destroy or blast-radius finding for that transient resource.\n- [ ] `rebar explain T10` renders the durable-infrastructure scope clause.\n- [ ] The regenerated T10 section in `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` renders the durable-infrastructure scope clause.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/plan_review/test_criteria_blocking.py -q`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide` and include the generated guide diff.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry validate-routing`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/rebar explain T10` and verify the rendered clause."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786551220368438001,"uuid":"4671eaa4-e433-4c86-a80d-c81a720554df"}